jei.roots.wildwood.desc=Once a sacred tree, the only remnant of these that remain in the world are their wildroots. From these a skilled wild mage, with the correct words and ingredients, can invoke the ritual of Wildroot Growth.
jei.roots.wildwood_sapling.desc=A rare, treasured young of a tree that does not itself bear children. No longer born, almost all of them have been secreted away by the druids of old.
jei.roots.wildwood_leaves.desc=Unlike the leaves of other trees, the sacred wildwood has no longer the strength to bear saplings. Instead, the kernel of life common to all parts of the wildwood - the wildroot - may be found tucked amongst its leaves and its branches.
jei.roots.elemental_soil_fire.desc=Created by tossing a piece of Elemental Soil into a pool of lava.
jei.roots.elemental_soil_water.desc=Created by tossing a piece of Elemental Soil into a pool of water and waiting a few seconds.
jei.roots.elemental_soil_air.desc=Created by dropping a piece of Elemental Soil onto a surface closer to the sky, and unobscured from it.
jei.roots.elemental_soil_earth.desc=Created by dropping a piece of Elemental Soil onto a surface covered from the sky and in the depth's of the ground.
jei.roots.open_book_button_text=Open Book
jei.roots.water_info=Must be adjacent to water
